    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/f1/probe.ts $PWD   # Bun.build of src/server/ui.ts, target bun, metafile on, with the release defines (LIMITLESS_BUILD_PACKAGED=true); counts metafile inputs under node_modules/@babel/ or babel-preset-solid/. Run again on a $TMPDIR copy of src/ and scripts/ with ui.ts replaced by the 1724e2f8 version.",
    "output": "head: success true inputs 295 babel 222 solid-plugin [ \"scripts/solid-plugin.ts\" ]\n1724e2f8 ui.ts: success true inputs 4 babel 0 solid-plugin []"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, src/server/ui.ts:3 imports `PACKAGED_BUILD` from release.ts and line 8 guards the dynamic import with `if (!PACKAGED_BUILD && info.kind === \"source\") { const { default: solidPlugin } = await import(\"../../scripts/solid-plugin.ts\"); ...`. release.ts defines `export const PACKAGED_BUILD = typeof LIMITLESS_BUILD_PACKAGED !== \"undefined\" && LIMITLESS_BUILD_PACKAGED;`. Bun 1.4.3 does not fold that constant across the module boundary, so the branch and all 222 Babel inputs stay in the bundle. The head test admits this: `// Known blocker: Bun 1.4.3 does not fold PACKAGED_BUILD across the release.ts export boundary ... test.failing(\"release defines remove the source UI compiler from the bundled server\", ...)`. scripts/build-binary.ts main() runs validateMetafile after compiling, and it throws on any @babel/ input and removes the binary, so a real build always fails. The issue requires that 'the release build removes [the branch] at compile time'. The implementer did stop and ask, as the issue told them to, but the code at head does not meet the requirement."
  },
