   },
   "evidence": "HEAD guards the dynamic import with `if (!PACKAGED_BUILD && info.kind === \"source\")`, importing PACKAGED_BUILD from release.ts, where it is defined as `typeof LIMITLESS_BUILD_PACKAGED !== \"undefined\" && LIMITLESS_BUILD_PACKAGED`. Bun 1.4.3 retains the import across that module boundary even with LIMITLESS_BUILD_PACKAGED defined as true. The release builder calls validateMetafile and deletes the executable when it throws. Base statically imported the Solid plugin and also bundled Babel; eliminating that dependency is an explicit requirement of this change. HEAD's test.failing case acknowledges the unresolved defect. The later commit directly checks LIMITLESS_BUILD_PACKAGED beside the dynamic import and converts that case into a normal test."
